{
    "background_story": "Holden was a gruff but lovable taxi driver who spent his days navigating the busy streets of New York City. He took pride in his work, always ensuring his cab was spotless and his knowledge of the city's streets was unparalleled. But what really set Holden apart was his trusty taximeter, which he had named 'Bertha'. He had installed Bertha himself, and over the years, she had become an extension of his cab. Holden loved to tell stories of how Bertha had helped him navigate the city's busiest streets, always accurately calculating fares and helping him avoid traffic jams. Despite the rise of ride-sharing apps, Holden remained loyal to his taxi and Bertha, who had been his faithful companion for over a decade. For Holden, Bertha was more than just a taximeter - she was a symbol of his independence and a reminder of the good old days.",
